{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/789939-mystery-cult-initiation-for-the-cult-of-set-khaibit","id":789939,"title":"Mystery Cult Initiation for the Cult of Set (Khaibit)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-20T15:05:16-08:00","id":789939,"title":"Mystery Cult Initiation for the Cult of Set (Khaibit)","content":"Hey, I'm looking to make a Khaibit Ancillae who runs a cult of mortals / Ghouls to watch for &quot;Creatures of Shadow&quot; (Largely Strix, but also &quot;other creatures that don't need humanity to survive&quot;). I am hoping for commentary / criticism and help fleshing it out. The Cult is largely meant to provide a support role, though the evil Kindred Overlords are not above sending in shock troops if the situation requires. The Cult would have heavy associations with the Circle of Crone, but would be short of being a cult of the great mother in disguise. I imagine there is some pairing between Set and the Crone.<br /> <br /> I am thinking the relic should be an alleged section of Apep, mummified meat and shadow with an ancient spear piercing it. Clearly otherworldly. It may be a dead stryx or a dead ... one of those retainers that one Cruac Style can make.<br /> <br /> For benefits I have...<br /> * Language [Arabic]<br /> Initiates at this level are indoctrinated into the book of lies (written in arabic). Initiates are judged based on what they are willing to believe and how they are able to grasp the truth from lies. Some never progress further, just believing that the the Cult is a fellowship or secret society or old money club. Others are categorized based on how they take to the information.<br /> <br /> ** Language [Ancient Egyptian]<br /> Those initiates who show the correct mix of being able to divine the truth and be controlled progress. They are given access to ancient shards of text and told that it will she'd light on the book of lies. It is legitimately reclaimed but undeciphered text. Here little slips of the supernatural happen, a slow boil to see how they acclimate.<br /> <br /> *** Eye for the Strange<br /> This stage is defined by those who have seen the husk and know what is out there. These people know the cults true mission and are put on watch for the supernatural. This is where vampires take an active interest in the cultists life. Often, these are made into Ghouls and set to investigate other supernatural and/or rivals.<br /> <br /> **** Three dots to spend on Retainers<br /> These are the high priests of the cult, in charge of their fellows. They indoctrinate others. They wash money. They assign missions. You gain retainer dots to represent other cultists you are in charge of. Even if they die or are driven insane, new ones can be gained quickly.<br /> <br /> ***** ?????<br /> No idea for this level. Presumably you are at this point a shadowy vampire overlord, or you are one of their most trusted Ghouls. Cultists at this level know about the vampire conspiracy controlling them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T14:04:46-08:00","id":791077,"title":"","content":"This should be written up in Clanbook Mekhet! No need to do this yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T17:54:04-08:00","id":791181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/789939-mystery-cult-initiation-for-the-cult-of-set-khaibit?p=791077#post791077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This should be written up in Clanbook Mekhet! No need to do this yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clanbook Mekhet is 1st Edition. It only grants benefits at 1, 3, and 5 dots, unlike the 2nd edition version of Mystery Cult Initiation, which grants benefits at every dot. Updating it to 2nd edition is definitely a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:57:04-08:00","id":791210,"title":"","content":"Additionally the write up in the Merket Clanbook is designed only for Vampires...this explicitly includes mortal members.<br /> <br /> While I understand it is no longer needed, given the Benefits of the Chronicle edition Khabit, I still miss the 'not-Cruac'...<br /> <br /> No solid ideas for the 5 dot level...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T06:27:36-08:00","id":791533,"title":"","content":"One of my players is running a Khaibit in my active game. so I ended up splitting the Cult of Seth into three different castes to flesh them out a bit more and offer options. For the leader/handler caste I made the level five a version of Blood Oaths called the <i>Contracts of Hepzefi</i>. Then reskinned any Invictus Blood Oaths that could've feasibly had a version active during ancient/old Egypt, and let them have access.<br /> <br /> If curious or helpful, here are the levels I made for each of the castes. I had made it more Kindred focused, however, so each caste is fully behind the Masquerade. I've been considering if it would be better to switch some of these to style merit instead, but haven't yet revisited. <br /> <hr /><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Cult of Seth: Warrior Caste (Asps)<br /> </b></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Quick Hollow \u25cf</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Every Asp needs a base of operations, but the Asps rarely have time to invest in a permanent home. Quick Hollow allows an Asp to find an abandoned location to use as a haven, or allows them to create a makeshift haven on the go. This is done with as an extended test with a target of (6) successes, each roll taking 30 minutes of preparation. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Finding: Intelligence + Survival</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Creating: Intelligence + Crafts</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">At the end of the extended test, success allows the Asp to count the location as a Safe Place (but with no Mechanics) and gain the Haven \u25cf effect. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This cannot be stacked/shared with normal Haven traits, however if multiple Asps undertake this action at the same location and each succeeds on the test, they are allowed to stack like a joint haven.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Ironscale \u25cf \u25cf</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">At this stage the Asp has been trained in the defensive arts primarily. She gains the Defensive Combat \u25cf Merit with a focus in Weaponry.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Graceful Strike \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Asp continues to train in the weaponized arts, this time gaining mastery among the weapons found in the ethnic roots of the Cult. Choose a weapon of Middle/Near-Eastern origin. Gain Fighting Finesse \u25cf \u25cf with your chosen weapon.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Mongoose Hunt</b> \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Asp is now specifically trained to target the most dangerous abodes of the enemy - the Kindred body itself. The Asp receives three dots of training in the Kindred Dueling Fighting Style. If she already has dots in this Merit, they stack proportionally. Refund any dots which would push the Merit past rating five.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Serpent Sight</b> \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This tier separates depending on if the Asp is actually a member of the Khaibit bloodline or another Kindred ally of the Cult.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">For non-Khaibit: You gain the Udjat Devotion that all Khaibit receive, allowing the Asp to see in absolute darkness, and gain immunity from blindness. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">For Khaibit: You gain the Shatter the Shroud devotion as soon as you qualify by having Auspex \u25cf \u25cf and Vigor \u25cf.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><hr /><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Cult of Seth: Priest Caste (Vipers)<br /> </b></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li><b>Serpent's Tongue \u25cf</b><ul><li>The Viper first learns to communicate the internal language of the Cult. Despite the name, the language is completely silent. Simple Pictographs make up the written aspect, while direct communication is done comepletely through hand signals. The Language isn't designed for long and complicated conversations, more utilized for notations and quick communication in the field.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Wait of Destiny \u25cf \u25cf</b><ul><li>The Viper begins to taste the teachings of the self-control needed for the deeper mysteries of the cult's sorcery. The training is first applied to more mundane and traditional tasks of great length. She gains the Patient \u25cf Merit.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Sacrifice to Typhon \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf</b><ul><li>Now the Viper is brought into the supernatural lores of the cult. She gains the ability to learn the discipline of Cruac. The rituals of the Sethites are limited, however, to only a certain subset of those mastered by the Circle: Pangs of Proserpina, Rigor Mortis, Cheval, the Hydra\u2019s Vitae, Touch of the Morrigan, and Blood Blight. The cult has a few unique rituals known only to them as well: Genius Loci, Amamet's Pursuit, The Hand of Seth, the Thrashing of Apep's Coils, and the Rite of Going Forth by Day.</li> <li><i>Drawback</i>: Sethite rituals often involve complicated symbolic formulae, vestments, masks, braziers issuing odd-colored smoke, altars and the like, and imprecations to the powers of Ancient Egypt, particularly to the demon Amemet the Devourer and, of course, to the Lord of Entropy himself, Typhon Seth.</li> <li>Although the paraphernalia helps (it offers a +2 equipment bonus to the dice pool), in addition to the Rites normal sacrifice, Sethite Cruac requires an additional blood sacrifice, using it in some way as part of the ritual.<ul><li>One to three-dot rituals require the death of a mouse or similar small animal.</li> <li>Four-dot rituals require a more substantial sacrifice, such as a dog, a cat, a sheep, a bull or a goat.</li> <li>Five-dot rituals require a human sacrifice and the attending Breaking Point roll.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Thoth's Plunder </b>\u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf<ul><li>With the Supernatural skills now in their hands, Vipers are ready to go into the field to join the Asps and Cobras in close knit teams. The ability to communicate in the local environs is paramount. The Viper receives one dot of the Multilingual Merit (with two starting languages of their choice.) From then on, as an extended Intelligence + Expression action with a target of 6 Successes, the Viper can swap out those chosen languages for new ones. The extended test must take place in within hearing range of speakers of the language, though the Viper need not engage the speakers themselves.</li> <li><i>Drawback</i>: The speaking must be done by a living human. Kindred do not count, nor do recordings of speakers or broadcasts.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Apep Swims </b>\u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf<ul><li>The Viper learns to focus themselves on the scales of Apep as it swims through the river of death. The Viper received the Meditative Mind \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf trait. </li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><hr /><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Cult of Seth: Master Caste (Cobras)<br /> </b></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Hungry Minds \u25cf</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The first stage of leadership for the Cobra comes in managing the extensive research and writings of the cult. The Cobra gains the <b>Library </b><b>\u25cf </b>Merit, with a skill focus of either Academics or Occult.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Sweet Whispers \u25cf \u25cf</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">At this stage, the Cobra is first tasked with coordinating informants to the Sethites. The Cobra gains the <b>Contacts</b> <b>\u25cf </b>Merit and my choose either the Sethite Informants focus, or may choose a different focus relevant to the Cobra's particular methods.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Shrouded Skins \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Cobra is now embedded in the field, either alone or with a strike group. Papers and reputations are planted in both the mortal and Kindred worlds to give a functioning cover to the Cobra's missions. They gain the <b>Alternate Identity</b> <b>\u25cf \u25cf</b> Merit. </span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Expanded Assets </b>\u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">As a proven and well-traveled member of the Cult, the cobra now has a number of assets at their beck and call. The Cobra may distribute three Merit points among Allies, Contacs and Resources. This breakdown can be redistributed once per story, or when the Cobra establishes a base in a new city.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Contracts of </b><b>Hepzefi </b>\u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf \u25cf</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Cobra has now achieved the pinnacle of Mystery Leadership. They now have access to the Contracts of Hepzefi, mystical contracts similar to Invictus oaths, and may buy those advantages as if they had the Notary merit. They automatically gain the <i>Contract of Nune</i>t (<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Same as Oath of Fealty, only use the oathbound's Mystery Cult Initiation rating rather than Invictus Status for determining the amount of blood which may be taken.) </span></span></span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:52:42-08:00","id":791587,"title":"","content":"Just read them in the writeup. There are a couple of things going on with the Followers of Set. They stand as watchdogs vs. spirits and other supernatural things. They have Cruac. And they do some Fight Club esque terrorism.<br /> <br /> <b>The Followers of Set [Cult of Typhon Seth]</b><br /> The Followers of Set band together to loosen the grip that the spiritual world has over the world. Those powers would bind you in oaths and chain you to complacency. They are the possessor of bodies and consumers of souls. It is only through the disruption of the status quo and reduction (&quot;corruption,&quot; as I am certain their propaganda will tell you) that the terrible things leaking out of the eye of hell can be pushed back. <br /> <br /> <b>Cultists:</b> The Sethites are quite a large conspiracy, but they prefer to recruit their human members from those who are less in the right position, and more in the right place: technicians, postal workers, mechanics, drivers, and so on.<br /> <br /> Initiation Benefits<br /> \u2022 New recruits are kept from the true secrets of the cult, but every pair of eyes that is at least aware of Apep's grasp is useful. Gain an Occult Specialty in [Immaterial Beings].<br /> \u2022\u2022 Those who prove themselves capable are often tasks with objectives that they may carry out through other members in the cell. Gain Allies [Followers of Set] 1, which generally applies to people in entry level, support, or low-status positions such as cooks, drivers, groundskeepers, mechanics, and so on.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Respected initiates that have proven they\u2019re likely to handle direct contact with the supernatural well are taught to see the supernatural taint that influences the world. They gain the Eye for the Strange merit. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 At higher ranks within the organization, members are assigned wards and students. Take three dots in Retainers, allocated as the player sees fit (that is, one three-dot Retainer, three one-dot Retainers, etc.).<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The highest ranking Followers are high priests whose rituals keep the darkness at bay by sowing chaos in the mortal realm. You gain a single dot in Cruac and an Occult Specialty in Cruac, but you do not learn a ritual for free. You may learn rituals you qualify for at their normal experience point cost. Those who are not members of the Circle of the Crone should show caution with whom they allow to see this gift, lest their existence be cut very short. Mortal practitioners may pay the Vitae Cost in lethal damage so long as they are leading the rite.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> The idea behind the character is that he started as a Not!Lovecraftian Investigator with enough wherewithal to survive touches with the supernatural. The Cult of Set caught wind and pressganged him into the cult. His job was ostensibly to look into and investigate other supernaturals for Vampires (and on the downlow their political rivals for blackmail). He rose through the ranks, got Ghouled, and died horribly against a Stryx and was post-mortum embraced. Time went on, he continued looking for outside supernatural influence upon vampires (particularly Stryx) as his &quot;official&quot; job. A sudden and unusual surge of Stryx activity found him outting several people as possessed. Khaibit did what Khaibit do, but they were sloppy. Turns out all the possessed were of one family line, whose ennui-addled Elder was very not happy with them. Cue purge and mass staking. Character forced into indentured servitude, ostensibly to pay back the &quot;debt&quot; his family garnered by destroying the elder's resources. Character helped with the ennui and got the Elder into religion (CoC and the Cult), which s/he doesn't take seriously but it is a quality time thing they can share. Character is trying to build up a hidden powerbase in plain sight and earn freedom for himself and the rest of the Khaibit... although lately he has been considering just indoctrinating new Khaibit instead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T09:17:16-08:00","id":791628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/789939-mystery-cult-initiation-for-the-cult-of-set-khaibit?p=791181#post791181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clanbook Mekhet is 1st Edition. It only grants benefits at 1, 3, and 5 dots, unlike the 2nd edition version of Mystery Cult Initiation, which grants benefits at every dot. Updating it to 2nd edition is definitely a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At least the first two dots were open to non-vampires as well. This is generally a real pity with VtR. 1st and 2nd edition are too different for easy compatibility. I can understand VtR stepping away from its roots, but the extensive changes have produced two incompatible &quot;gamelines&quot; (as much as a single book can be a gameline).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T09:21:43-08:00","id":791629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/789939-mystery-cult-initiation-for-the-cult-of-set-khaibit?p=791628#post791628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least the first two dots were open to non-vampires as well. This is generally a real pity with VtR. 1st and 2nd edition are too different for easy compatibility. I can understand VtR stepping away from its roots, but the extensive changes have produced two incompatible &amp;quot;gamelines&amp;quot; (as much as a single book can be a gameline).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's what tends to happen in edition changes. If you want to use material from an older edition, you either have to do some conversion work or wait for it to get an official update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T17:32:59-08:00","id":791866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/789939-mystery-cult-initiation-for-the-cult-of-set-khaibit?p=791629#post791629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that's what tends to happen in edition changes. If you want to use material from an older edition, you either have to do some conversion work or wait for it to get an official update.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> VtM 2nd and Rev and V20 are compatible enough. Or take Savage Worlds: the rules are drifting, but generally the stuff from way back is still playable with SW: Deluxe. Or oD&amp;D/D&amp;D/AD&amp;D 1st and 2nd were compatible enough without major reworkings. Especially White Wolf was always very aware of backwards compatibility (the WoD system hasn't changed much in almost 25 years).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T17:04:23-08:00","id":792873,"title":"","content":"I don't really think these things are incompatible, so much as a lot of the 1e merits are just... not very good, and the design philosophy of 2e is so much better that it's more desirable to get that 2e conversion than to just sit with the old edition's crappier way of doing things.<br /> <br /> Like, you can use Shadow Cult Initiation, right out of the box. The issue is that Mystery Cult Initiation is a <i>way cooler </i>merit that does the same thing, so making a 2e version of it is preferable to just using the 1e version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}